"""Editorial question designs for asteroid resources and speculative contact."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


ASTEROID = """history_origins|From Asteroid Survey to Resource Proposal|How did science missions inform mining concepts?|Trace dated studies and actual missions.
famous_examples|A Sample-Return Mission|What material was measured and what does it not prove about extraction?|Use mission and laboratory data.
hidden_stories|Labor in Space Resource Plans|Which prospecting, ground-control, and processing roles are omitted?|Map a proposed operation.
beginner_explainers|Prospecting versus Mining|What separates remote sensing, sampling, extraction, and product delivery?|Define each stage.
advanced_concepts|Ore Grade in Microgravity|How would composition, particle size, and processing yield affect viability?|Use target-specific measurements.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Valuable Asteroid Claim|What evidence would establish recoverable value after mission costs?|Specify commodity and market.
technology_innovation|An Extraction Prototype|What throughput, energy, and material purity were demonstrated?|Distinguish lab from flight.
people_personalities|A Mission Designer's Choices|Which tradeoffs shaped a prospecting concept?|Use attributed technical records.
major_events|A Space-Resources Policy Decision|How did a dated legal or program decision change plans?|Read primary text and scope.
how_it_works|From Asteroid to Useful Product|How do survey, rendezvous, capture, processing, and delivery connect?|Trace mass and energy.
rise_fall|A Mining Venture's Change of Course|Which technical, financing, or demand assumption failed?|Use filings and dated statements.
then_vs_now|Resource Concepts across Decades|Which capabilities became real and which remain proposals?|Compare mission evidence.
future_developments|Conditional Asteroid Industry|What repeated demand and low-cost logistics would be required?|Model scenarios, not forecasts.
myths_vs_facts|Trillions in One Asteroid?|How do hypothetical metal prices differ from recoverable revenue?|Include supply and market effects.
documentary_stories|A Prospector Concept's Trail|How did targets, testing, budget, and status change?|Build dated source record.
assumption_inventory|An Asteroid-Mining Business Case|Which grade, yield, transport, law, and buyer assumptions matter?|Show sensitivity.
readiness_check|Before an Extraction Mission|Are target characterization and processing tests adequate?|Set mission-specific criteria.
physical_limits|Trajectory, Gravity, and Power|How do delta-v, spin, thermal conditions, and sunlight constrain work?|Use target orbit.
governance_choice|Rules for Space Resources|Which activities are allowed or disputed under applicable law?|Distinguish treaty from proposals.
unequal_futures|Who Gets Space-Resource Benefits?|How are public science, private rights, and risks distributed?|Compare governance options.
scenario_pair|Water for Space versus Metals for Earth|How do customers and transport economics differ?|Hold target and technology clear.
failure_to_launch|A Mission without a Buyer|Which demand or financing gap blocked development?|Use documented project outcome.
unintended_effect|Activity around a Small Body|Could extraction harm scientific records or create debris?|Assess mission footprint.
social_adaptation|A New Space Supply Chain|Which institutions would need to coordinate safety and trade?|Bound to a scenario.
ethical_boundary|Science Access versus Extraction|When should a target be studied before disturbance?|State preservation criteria.
signal_vs_hype|Survey Data versus Mine Output|What evidence proves produced usable material?|Separate sample return from industry.
reversible_steps|An Extraction Trial's Exit|How can equipment and debris be managed if it fails?|Use mission disposal plan.
field_resource_budget|Asteroid-Mining Mass Balance|How much input yields deliverable product?|Include waste and propellant.
field_habitat_design|Human Presence at a Target?|Is crew habitation justified against robotic work?|Compare risk and task.
field_governance_model|Who Authorizes Extraction?|How do state supervision and international obligations apply?|Name operator and jurisdiction.
field_dependency_chain|A Processing Failure in Space|Which downstream deliveries depend on one stage?|Map backup suppliers.
field_social_inclusion|Voice in Space-Resource Policy|Who participates in rule-making and who is absent?|Read consultation records.
"""

INTERSTELLAR = """history_origins|Interstellar Settlement Ideas|How did probe concepts become civilization narratives?|Separate scientific study and fiction.
famous_examples|Voyager beyond the Heliosphere|What does its journey demonstrate about distance and time?|Use NASA mission facts.
hidden_stories|Generations behind a Starflight Concept|Who would build, maintain, and inherit its risks?|Identify assumed labor and consent.
beginner_explainers|Interstellar Space versus Another Star|Why does crossing the heliopause not mean reaching a star?|Compare distances.
advanced_concepts|Energy for Starflight|How do payload mass, cruise speed, and propulsion change energy demand?|State model assumptions.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Habitable Destination?|Which exoplanet observations could test conditions for settlement?|Separate detection from surface knowledge.
technology_innovation|A Proposed Interstellar Propulsion System|What has been tested at relevant scale?|Distinguish component and mission.
people_personalities|A Scientist's Starflight Vision|Which assumptions underlie one proposal?|Read primary study and critiques.
major_events|An Interstellar Probe Milestone|What was observed beyond the Sun's plasma influence?|Use mission telemetry.
how_it_works|A Starflight Mission Architecture|How do acceleration, cruise, braking, power, and communication connect?|Map each stage.
rise_fall|A Starship Proposal Revised|Which energy, budget, or material limit forced change?|Compare dated designs.
then_vs_now|Voyager and New Probe Concepts|How do achievable mission goals differ?|State distance and mission type.
future_developments|Conditional Paths to Another Star|Which propulsion and life-support breakthroughs would be needed?|Avoid dated arrival promises.
myths_vs_facts|Interstellar Probe Equals Starship?|What target does a heliosphere probe actually reach?|Use mission objective.
documentary_stories|One Starflight Study's Evolution|How did assumptions and criticism alter the design?|Follow primary technical record.
assumption_inventory|A Multi-Generation Voyage|Which autonomy, biology, repair, and governance premises are required?|Expose untested claims.
readiness_check|Before Launching a Star Probe|Are power, navigation, communication, and longevity credible?|Use demonstrated lifetimes.
physical_limits|Distance and Signal Delay|What do light speed and travel time impose on coordination?|Calculate for a named target.
governance_choice|Authority across Generations|Who can alter mission goals when descendants cannot consent now?|Compare governance designs.
unequal_futures|Who Bears Starflight Costs?|Which generations fund, travel, or lose alternatives?|Use explicit ethical scenario.
scenario_pair|Robotic Probe versus Crewed Ark|How do goals, mass, risk, and data differ?|Hold destination fixed.
failure_to_launch|A Concept without Enabling Technology|Which untested propulsion or habitat element blocks launch?|Use readiness levels.
unintended_effect|Launching toward an Unknown World|Could arrival disturb possible life or scientific evidence?|Apply planetary-protection questions.
social_adaptation|Society on a Long Voyage|What institutions would cope with isolation and change?|Mark as speculative worldbuilding.
ethical_boundary|Consent of Future Travelers|Can descendants reject a mission they inherit?|Examine reversible choices.
signal_vs_hype|An Interstellar Mission Claim|Is the craft merely beyond the heliosphere or bound for a star?|State trajectory.
reversible_steps|Can a Mission Turn Back?|Which decisions are irreversible after acceleration?|Map decision points.
field_resource_budget|Starship Energy and Material Ledger|What mass and power does a given design assume?|Include shielding and repair.
field_habitat_design|A Long-Voyage Habitat|How would radiation, gravity, food, and maintenance be supplied?|Use explicit duration.
field_governance_model|A Society beyond Earth Contact|How would authority and succession work?|Tie scenario to communication delay.
field_dependency_chain|Failure over Many Generations|Which system losses cannot be replaced?|Stress-test spares and knowledge.
field_social_inclusion|Who Chooses an Interstellar Future?|Which present and future people have a voice?|Avoid treating one vision as universal.
"""

CONTACT = """history_origins|First-Contact Stories across Eras|How did a named work reflect its period's fears and hopes?|Use dated text and context.
famous_examples|One Contact Narrative|What rule defines the encounter and how is it revealed?|Analyze a specific work.
hidden_stories|Whose Voice Is Missing at Contact?|Which people interpret events without authority to speak?|Check point of view.
beginner_explainers|Signal, Biosignature, or Encounter?|How do different discoveries change a story?|Define evidence and distance.
advanced_concepts|Communication without Shared Assumptions|What could be misunderstood before language is learned?|Design an interpretable scene.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Signal That Might Be Noise|What independent checks would a plausible story require?|Use SETI verification principles.
technology_innovation|Detection Tool as Plot Device|What instrument can reveal a clue and what are its limits?|Ground in actual method.
people_personalities|A Character Facing Uncertainty|How do expertise and bias affect interpretation?|Show choices and correction.
major_events|The Announcement Moment|Who verifies and shares evidence in the story?|Model public consequences.
how_it_works|From Anomaly to Confirmation|What sequence of observation and independent replication is plausible?|Avoid instant certainty.
rise_fall|A False Contact Alarm|How does the story reveal an ordinary cause?|Keep clues fair to audience.
then_vs_now|Contact Stories and Changing Science|Which assumptions aged and which remain useful?|Compare versions or periods.
future_developments|After Confirmed Detection|What social paths follow different evidence types?|Branch without claiming prediction.
myths_vs_facts|What Real SETI Can Tell Us|Can a signal reveal biology, motive, or location?|Separate data and inference.
documentary_stories|A Fictional Detection Dossier|Which logs, debates, and announcements reveal the event?|Use internally consistent dates.
assumption_inventory|A Contact Scenario's Rules|Which distance, biology, technology, and intent premises are invented?|Label speculation.
readiness_check|Before a Public Claim|Have alternate explanations and independent observations been tested?|Use current SETI guidance.
physical_limits|Light-Speed Communication|How does distance alter dialogue and action?|Calculate delay for a chosen system.
governance_choice|Who Speaks for Earth?|How do institutions and publics contest a reply?|Show authority limits.
unequal_futures|Uneven Effects of Contact News|Who gains information or power while others face fear or exclusion?|Use varied characters.
scenario_pair|Signal versus Arrival|How do verification and immediate safety differ?|Hold society fixed.
failure_to_launch|A Message Never Sent|What technical or political conflict blocks a response?|Show decision chain.
unintended_effect|A Premature Announcement|What harm follows a weak claim amplified as certainty?|Trace correction and trust.
social_adaptation|Everyday Life after Detection|How do schools, faith groups, and media respond differently?|Avoid one global reaction.
ethical_boundary|Speaking for Another Species|When does human projection distort interpretation?|Make uncertainty visible.
signal_vs_hype|Evidence in a Contact Story|Which observation supports each character's claim?|Distinguish clue from proof.
reversible_steps|A Response Decision|Which actions can be delayed while evidence improves?|Identify irreversible broadcast.
field_world_rule|Contact's Governing Rule|What can each side perceive and exchange?|Keep scenes consistent.
field_plausibility_boundary|Where Science Ends and Invention Begins|Which premise is speculative and what follows logically?|Disclose in story notes.
field_point_of_view|The First Witness|How does limited knowledge shape what the reader learns?|Avoid omniscient certainty.
field_ethical_consequence|A Choice with Real Cost|Who bears the cost of announcing or replying?|Trace consequences.
field_adaptation_choice|Different Contact Media|How must discovery change between prose, audio, and film?|Preserve evidence chain.
"""

if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("478", "478_asteroid_mining", ASTEROID,
                  "Asteroid mining through measured material, extraction and delivery stages, economics, law, and environmental stewardship.",
                  "NASA sample-return records and resource concept studies, target characterization, technical trials, company filings, and UN space-resource deliberations",
                  "Name target, commodity, destination, and project stage. Composition or theoretical market value does not prove recoverable profit.")
    revise_domain("479", "479_interstellar_civilization", INTERSTELLAR,
                  "Interstellar civilization through observed heliosphere exploration, vast starflight distances, unproven propulsion and biology, and intergenerational governance.",
                  "NASA Voyager mission data and interstellar-probe studies, exoplanet observations, technical concept papers, and space-law sources",
                  "Name destination, distance, speed, and mission type. Crossing the heliopause is not visiting another star; settlement remains speculative.")
    revise_domain("480", "480_first_contact", CONTACT,
                  "First contact as evidence-aware speculative storytelling about detection, verification, communication limits, public response, and moral choice.",
                  "IAA/SETI post-detection principles, observational methods, primary works of contact fiction, and authorial or archival context",
                  "Distinguish fiction from present evidence. A candidate signal is not confirmed extraterrestrial intelligence and no single character speaks for humanity.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
